## Window Runtime Methods

### Basic Window Control

```lua
Window:Open()
Window:Close()
Window:Toggle()
Window:Destroy()
Window:ToggleFullscreen()
Window:SetToTheCenter()
```

### Window Text/Icon/Size

```lua
Window:SetTitle("New Title")
Window:SetAuthor("by someone")
Window:SetIconSize(24) -- number or UDim2
Window:SetSize(UDim2.fromOffset(700, 500))
Window:SetToggleKey(Enum.KeyCode.RightShift)
```

### Background Runtime Methods

```lua
Window:SetBackgroundVideo("1234567890")
Window:SetBackgroundVideo("video:rbxassetid://1234567890")
Window:SetBackgroundImage("rbxassetid://987654321")
Window:SetBackgroundImageTransparency(0.35)
Window:SetBackgroundTransparency(0.2)
```

Returns:

- `SetBackgroundVideo(video)` returns `boolean`.
- `SetBackgroundImage(image)` returns `boolean`.
- transparency methods return `true/false` in source or nil in docs depending method/version.

### Resizing, Scale, Panel, Transparency

```lua
Window:IsResizable(true)
Window:SetUIScale(0.85)
local scale = Window:GetUIScale()
Window:ToggleTransparency(true)
Window:SetPanelBackground(true)
Window:SetPanelBackgroundVisible(true)
Window:SetPanelBackgroundHidden(false)
```

`Window:SetPanelBackground(value)` in source treats booleans with compatibility behavior. For new code, prefer:

```lua
Window:SetPanelBackgroundVisible(true)
Window:SetPanelBackgroundHidden(false)
```

### Locking Elements

Official docs mention:

```lua
Window:LockAllElements()
Window:UnlockAllElements()
Window:GetAllElements()
```

The provided source exposes:

```lua
Window:LockAll()
Window:UnlockAll()
Window:GetLocked()
Window:GetUnlocked()
```

For agents, prefer the source-observed names unless the user’s Shiny version explicitly documents aliases.

### Event Triggers

```lua
Window:OnOpen(function() end)
Window:OnClose(function() end)
Window:OnDestroy(function() end)
```

### Tabs and Sections

```lua
local Tab = Window:Tab({ Title = "Main" })
Window:SelectTab(Tab)
local allTabs = Window:GetTabs()

local TabSection = Window:Section({ Title = "Combat", Opened = true })
local CombatTab = TabSection:Tab({ Title = "Aimbot" })
```

### Topbar and Close Buttons

```lua
Window:DisableTopbarButtons({ "Close", "Minimize" })
```

Source-level topbar button method uses positional arguments internally:

```lua
Window:CreateTopbarButton(
    "Button Name",
    "icon-name",
    function() end,
    996, -- layout order
    true, -- icon themed
    Color3.fromHex("#60C762"),
    16 -- icon size
)
```

Use cautiously because this is lower-level than normal element APIs.

