## Key System

Key system is defined inside `CreateWindow` config.

### API Service Key System

```lua
local Window = WindUI:CreateWindow({
    Title = "Protected Hub",
    Folder = "ProtectedHub",
    KeySystem = {
        Note = "Get a key using one of the supported services.",
        API = {
            { Type = "platoboost", ServiceId = 1234, Secret = "secret" },
            { Type = "pandadevelopment", ServiceId = "id" },
            { Type = "luarmor", ScriptId = "script_id", Discord = "https://discord.gg/example" },
        },
        SaveKey = true,
    },
})
```

### Supported Services

Documented:

- `platoboost`
- `pandadevelopment`
- `luarmor`

Observed in source:

- `junkiedevelopment`

Service registry format:

```lua
WindUI.Services.myservice = {
    Name = "My Service",
    Icon = "droplet",
    Args = { "ServiceId" },
    New = function(ServiceId)
        return {
            Verify = function(key)
                return key == "valid", "message"
            end,
            Copy = function()
                setclipboard("https://example.com/get-key")
            end,
        }
    end,
}
```

### Custom `KeyValidator`

Although Shiny emphasizes service APIs, source compatibility supports `KeyValidator`:

```lua
KeySystem = {
    Title = "Access Required",
    Note = "Enter the correct key.",
    KeyValidator = function(key)
        return key == "HelloWorld"
    end,
    SaveKey = true,
}
```

### Key URL and Thumbnail

```lua
KeySystem = {
    Note = "Click Get Key to copy the link.",
    URL = "https://discord.gg/example",
    KeyValidator = function(key)
        return key == "secret"
    end,
    SaveKey = true,
    Thumbnail = {
        Image = "rbxassetid://123456789",
        Title = "Premium Access",
        Width = 200,
    },
}
```

### Key Save Behavior

When `SaveKey = true`, Shiny stores keys under:

```text
[Window.Folder or Temp]/[hwid/userId].key
```

The source validates saved keys on future loads.

### Agent Guidance

- Prefer `KeyValidator` for simple keys.
- Prefer `API = {...}` for third-party key services.
- Avoid hard-coding real service secrets in public code examples.
- The old `KeySystem.Key` path exists in source for compatibility, but agents should prefer `KeyValidator` or service `API`.

