## Dialogs

Window dialogs are modal prompts attached to a window.

```lua
local Dialog = Window:Dialog({
    Icon = "bird",
    IconThemed = true,
    Title = "Dialog Title",
    Content = "Dialog content",
    Buttons = {
        { Title = "Confirm", Variant = "Primary", Callback = function() end },
        { Title = "Cancel", Variant = "Secondary", Callback = function() end },
    },
})
```

Documented methods:

```lua
Dialog:Show()
Dialog:Close()
```

Source note: Shiny’s dialog creation opens the dialog immediately and returns an internal dialog object with `Open()`/`Close()` behavior. For portability, treat `Window:Dialog({...})` as showing immediately unless your version documents otherwise.

Button options:

| Key | Type |
|---|---|
| `Title` | `string` |
| `Icon` | `string?` |
| `Variant` | `string?` — `Primary`, `Secondary`, `Tertiary`, etc. |
| `Callback` | `function?` |

