## Config System

Configs save and load element states for elements with a `Flag`.

### Setup

```lua
local Window = WindUI:CreateWindow({
    Title = "Config Demo",
    Folder = "ConfigDemo",
})

local ConfigManager = Window.ConfigManager
local MyConfig = ConfigManager:CreateConfig("myConfig")

Tab:Toggle({
    Title = "Toggle",
    Flag = "ToggleElement",
    Callback = function() end,
})
```

### Config Path

Source-observed path:

```text
WindUI/[Window.Folder]/config/[configName].json
```

Note: Original WindUI used `configs/`; Shiny/Boreal source uses singular `config/`.

### ConfigManager Methods

```lua
local ConfigManager = Window.ConfigManager

local cfg = ConfigManager:CreateConfig("default", false)
local cfg2 = ConfigManager:Config("other", true) -- alias for CreateConfig
ConfigManager:SetPath("Custom/Path")
local names = ConfigManager:AllConfigs()
local existing = ConfigManager:GetConfig("default")
local autoload = ConfigManager:GetAutoLoadConfigs()
ConfigManager:DeleteConfig("old")
```

### Config Object Methods

```lua
cfg:SetAsCurrent()
cfg:Register("flag", element)
cfg:Unregister("flag")
cfg:Set("customKey", "customValue")
local custom = cfg:Get("customKey")
cfg:SetAutoLoad(true)
cfg:Save()
cfg:Load()
cfg:Delete()
local data = cfg:GetData()
```

### Saveable Element Types

Source parser supports:

- `Colorpicker`
- `Dropdown`
- `Segmented`
- `Input`
- `Keybind`
- `ButtonKeybind`
- `Slider`
- `Stepper`
- `Progress`
- `Stats`
- `Toggle`
- `ToggleKeybind`

### Config Example

```lua
local ConfigTab = Window:Tab({ Title = "Configs", Icon = "folder" })
local ConfigName = "default"
local ConfigManager = Window.ConfigManager

local NameInput = ConfigTab:Input({
    Title = "Config Name",
    Value = ConfigName,
    Callback = function(value)
        ConfigName = value
    end,
})

local ConfigList = ConfigTab:Dropdown({
    Title = "Available Configs",
    Values = ConfigManager:AllConfigs(),
    Callback = function(value)
        ConfigName = value
        NameInput:Set(value)
    end,
})

ConfigTab:Button({
    Title = "Save Config",
    Icon = "save",
    Callback = function()
        local cfg = ConfigManager:CreateConfig(ConfigName)
        cfg:Save()
        if ConfigList.Refresh then
            ConfigList:Refresh(ConfigManager:AllConfigs())
        end
        WindUI:Notify({ Title = "Saved", Content = "Config saved.", Icon = "check" })
    end,
})

ConfigTab:Button({
    Title = "Load Config",
    Icon = "refresh-cw",
    Callback = function()
        local cfg = ConfigManager:CreateConfig(ConfigName)
        local result, err = cfg:Load()
        if result == false then
            WindUI:Notify({ Title = "Load Failed", Content = tostring(err), Icon = "x" })
        else
            WindUI:Notify({ Title = "Loaded", Content = "Config loaded.", Icon = "check" })
        end
    end,
})
```

### Config Best Practices

- Always set `Folder` on the window.
- Every saveable element should have a unique `Flag`.
- Avoid duplicate flags; the latest element may overwrite flag lookup.
- File APIs are required: `writefile`, `readfile`, `isfile`, `isfolder`, `makefolder`, etc.
- Config does not work in normal Roblox Studio without executor file APIs.

