## Flag Runtime API

WindUI Shiny source adds direct flag inspection and mutation APIs on `Window`.

```lua
local element = Window:GetFlagElement("feature_enabled")
local value = Window:GetFlag("feature_enabled")
local ok, err = Window:SetFlag("feature_enabled", true)
local flags = Window:ListFlags()
local hasFlag = Window:HasFlag("feature_enabled")
local values = Window:GetFlags()
local results = Window:SetFlags({
    feature_enabled = true,
    power_slider = 80,
})
```

Methods:

| Method | Description |
|---|---|
| `GetFlagElement(flag)` | Returns element object for flag or nil. |
| `GetFlag(flag)` | Returns current element value/default. |
| `SetFlag(flag, value, ...)` | Calls element `Set`, `Select`, or `Update` if supported. |
| `ListFlags()` | Returns sorted flag names. |
| `HasFlag(flag)` | Boolean flag existence. |
| `GetFlags()` | Returns map of all flag values. |
| `SetFlags(table, ...)` | Applies many flags; returns `{ Applied = {}, Failed = {} }`. |

